HeaderInclude
config/emex64/emex64-opts.h

mcpu=
Target RejectNegative Joined Enum(emex64_cpu) Var(emex64_cpu) Init(EMEX64_CPU_DEFAULT)
-mcpu=CPU	Generate code for CPU: generic, emex64-v17, emex64-v18, emex64-v19, emex64-v20, emex64-v21, emex64e, emex64e-v20 or emex64e-v21.

Enum
Name(emex64_cpu) Type(enum emex64_cpu_type)
Known emex64 CPUs (for use with the -mcpu= option):

EnumValue
Enum(emex64_cpu) String(generic) Value(EMEX64_CPU_GENERIC)

EnumValue
Enum(emex64_cpu) String(emex64-v17) Value(EMEX64_CPU_V17)

EnumValue
Enum(emex64_cpu) String(emex64-v18) Value(EMEX64_CPU_V18)

EnumValue
Enum(emex64_cpu) String(emex64-v19) Value(EMEX64_CPU_V19)

EnumValue
Enum(emex64_cpu) String(emex64-v20) Value(EMEX64_CPU_V20)

EnumValue
Enum(emex64_cpu) String(emex64e) Value(EMEX64_CPU_EMEX64E)

EnumValue
Enum(emex64_cpu) String(emex64e-v20) Value(EMEX64_CPU_EMEX64E_V20)

EnumValue
Enum(emex64_cpu) String(emex64-v21) Value(EMEX64_CPU_V21)

EnumValue
Enum(emex64_cpu) String(emex64e-v21) Value(EMEX64_CPU_EMEX64E_V21)

march=
Target RejectNegative Joined Enum(emex64_arch) Var(emex64_arch) Init(EMEX64_CPU_NONE)
-march=ISA	Generate code for ISA: la64-v17, la64-v18, la64-v19, la64-v20, la64-v21, la64e-v19, la64e-v20 or la64e-v21 (e: pointer authentication); wins over -mcpu.

Enum
Name(emex64_arch) Type(enum emex64_cpu_type)
Known emex64 ISAs (for use with the -march= option):

EnumValue
Enum(emex64_arch) String(la64-v17) Value(EMEX64_CPU_V17)

EnumValue
Enum(emex64_arch) String(la64-v18) Value(EMEX64_CPU_V18)

EnumValue
Enum(emex64_arch) String(la64-v19) Value(EMEX64_CPU_V19)

EnumValue
Enum(emex64_arch) String(la64-v20) Value(EMEX64_CPU_V20)

EnumValue
Enum(emex64_arch) String(la64e-v19) Value(EMEX64_CPU_EMEX64E)

EnumValue
Enum(emex64_arch) String(la64e-v20) Value(EMEX64_CPU_EMEX64E_V20)

EnumValue
Enum(emex64_arch) String(la64-v21) Value(EMEX64_CPU_V21)

EnumValue
Enum(emex64_arch) String(la64e-v21) Value(EMEX64_CPU_EMEX64E_V21)

msoft-float
Target RejectNegative Mask(SOFT_FLOAT)
Do not use the floating point unit; float and double are passed like integers.

mhard-float
Target RejectNegative InverseMask(SOFT_FLOAT)
Use the floating point unit (ISA v18 and later).

mbranch-protection=
Target RejectNegative Joined Var(emex64_branch_protection_string)
-mbranch-protection=none|standard|pac-ret[+leaf]	Sign return addresses (emex64e).
